# FABLE-SONNET-OCC-ROOT-20260924-146: an own-field occurrence under a NAMED (method) root,
# `test\[N]field`, resolved by the same occurrence lookup the rootless `\[N]field` form uses
# (l2_own_find_occ) -- no second scanner.
#
# Q29 (author, 2026-09-25; FABLE-OPUS-CODE-DATA-SPLIT-20260925-189 c3c): the two bare assignments
# of `arg` are one cell -- `\[N]` numbers declarations, and a repeated bare assignment is not an
# occurrence.  So test\[0]arg and testrg read that one cell, 2; test\[1]arg names nothing (the
# refusal is unit_occ_arg_second_refused.lm2).
fn: test (int: arg) int
    arg: 1
    arg: 2
    return: 0
end: test

int: got
got: test(0)
if: test\[0]arg != 2
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 81; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
if: test\arg != 2
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 83; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 0; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
